# Gap Analysis and Data Discovery Findings

Pop Culture Clothing Website, Capstone B, Sprint 1
Prepared by: Capstone B project team

## Summary

Comparing our Week 2 inventory (21 items) with the industry systems
(Amazon, Kmart Online and Cotton On) showed that we had covered the core
product, account, cart and order data. However, we were missing data that
customers rely on to make and trust a purchase.

## Missing data items

| New data item | Why customers need it | Where it is used |
|---|---|---|
| Size and colour variants | Lets customers choose the right option and see availability | Product page |
| Size guides | Helps customers pick the correct size | Product page |
| Reviews and ratings | Builds trust in the product | Product page |
| Estimated delivery date | Sets clear delivery expectations | Product page and checkout |
| Shipping cost | Shows the total price before payment | Cart and checkout |
| Return and refund policy | Reduces uncertainty before buying | Product page and checkout |
| Promo codes | Lets customers apply discounts | Cart |
| Order history | Lets customers review past orders | Customer account |
| Tracking number with courier | Lets customers follow their delivery | Customer account and order details |

## Risk and validation

Our risk analysis showed that price, stock and cart total need server-side
validation. Industry sites reinforce this by showing live stock and delivery
information.

## Inputs for the Week 4 database design

We will add tables or fields for:

- `variants`
- `reviews`
- `promo_codes`
- `order_history`
- `tracking_number`

## Access control and reporting

- Admin-only data such as revenue and customer lists will be protected with
  role-based access control.
- Best-selling products and low-stock alerts were identified as useful
  dashboard reports.
